  "id": "acoustic-filter",
  "term": "acoustic filter",
  "definition": "An acoustic filter is a structure designed to control how sound waves pass through a system by selectively reflecting, absorbing, or reducing certain wave components. In the source material, it refers to a multilayer duct arrangement that uses porous material and flexible membranes to tune sound attenuation, especially at low frequencies.",
